  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Rights Due Dilligence Knowledge and Experience Exchange for Trade Unions, Freedom of Association and Collective Bargaining</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mondiaal FNV  will build on its expertise and existing networks of trade unions,  and other industrial stakeholders bringing European and production country stakeholders together to exchange knowledge, increase transparency regarding socio-environmental impact on workers, including better wages, safer workplaces and increased access to social security.  Together will unlock and use this (local) knowledge, local approaches and best practices - both in the form of HRDD relevant information, and as evidence and input for advocacy - to influence business as well as public policies and practices. Making validated stakeholder information and lessons learned accessible in a structured way to influence industry action, through i.e. the HRDD Dashboard and other tools, is a central element in this effort. In production countries, we aim to make key public and private decision-makers see that reducing human rights risks through social dialogue improves economic opportunities in a global marketplace that increasingly follows HRDD.</narrative>
  </description>
